  "_provenance": "Two REAL serialized (BlockHash, ChannelMonitor) blobs, in LDK's own on-disk monitor format, for two 100 000-sat channels between LDK's deterministic functional-test nodes. Regenerate with a throwaway crate depending on lightning 0.2.4 with the \"_test_utils\" feature: create_chanmon_cfgs(2) / create_node_cfgs / create_node_chanmgrs / create_network, create_announced_chan_between_nodes(&nodes, 0, 1) twice, then hex(nodes[0].chain_monitor.chain_monitor.get_monitor(chan_id).unwrap().encode()). The funding txids are fixed by the harness's deterministic keys, so the vectors are stable.",
  "_why": "Nothing in this crate can mint a ChannelMonitor offline (a real funded channel is required), yet restore's fund-safety guard is 'validate by deserialization'. These blobs let the restore tests exercise the REAL validation path instead of a stub. LDK re-derives signer key material from channel_keys_id on read and skips the serialized signer bytes, so a monitor written by any node deserializes under any seed's KeysManager/SignerProvider: the seed proof on the restore path is the successful DECRYPT of the VSS blob (the encryption key is seed-derived), and these vectors deliberately exercise the format half.",
